---
import '../styles/landing-v2.css';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const { whatsappNumber, whatsappMessage, seo, siteUrl, brandName } = siteConfig;
const whatsappUrl = `https://wa.me/${whatsappNumber}?text=${encodeURIComponent(whatsappMessage)}`;
const canonicalUrl = `${siteUrl}/`;
const ogImageUrl = `${siteUrl}/og-image.svg`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>{seo.title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={seo.description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />

    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={seo.title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={seo.description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content={brandName} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImageUrl} />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />

    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={seo.title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={seo.description} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImageUrl} />

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="anonymous" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@graph': [
        {
          '@type': 'Organization',
          name: brandName,
          url: canonicalUrl
        },
        {
          '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
          name: brandName,
          applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication',
          operatingSystem: 'Web',
          description: seo.description,
          url: canonicalUrl,
          offers: {
            '@type': 'Offer',
            price: '29.99',
            priceCurrency: 'GBP'
          }
        }
      ]
    })} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="wrap">
      <header class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Trade Forge <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> tradeforge.uk</p>
        <h1>WhatsApp is already<br />your <span>job book.</span><br />Let's make it tax-ready.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          Customers keep messaging the way they always have. You get bookings, a live view of every job,
          and clean records ready for your accountant and HMRC.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={whatsappUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Join the waitlist on WhatsApp
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">First 100 sign-ups get 3 months free <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> £29.99/month after</p>
      </header>

      <section class="costs" aria-labelledby="costs-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="costs-title">What it actually costs you</h2>
          <p>Not abstract market size. The money that slips away every week.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stats">
          <article class="stat"><strong>78%</strong><span>of customers book whoever replies first</span></article>
          <article class="stat"><strong>43%</strong><span>of enquiries never get a reply at all</span></article>
          <article class="stat"><strong>£150 to £350</strong><span>lost for every job-day that slips to a competitor</span></article>
          <article class="stat"><strong>£200</strong><span>HMRC fine once MTD penalty points hit four</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="pillars" aria-labelledby="pillars-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="pillars-title">Three jobs, one chat thread</h2>
          <p>Everything Trade Forge does serves one of these: no new app, no training, no admin evening.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillars">
          <article class="pillar">
            <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <h3>Frictionless WhatsApp booking</h3>
            <p>Enquiries become booked jobs inside the chat. Quote in a couple of clicks, customer accepts on WhatsApp, slot's confirmed. No back-and-forth.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <h3>Every job, booked to paid</h3>
            <p>Booked → Scheduled → Completed → Due → Paid. One-tap status updates from site, invoices sent as a PDF the day the work's done.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <h3>Making Tax Digital exports</h3>
            <p>Paid jobs and receipt photos become tax-ready digital records: a quarterly export instead of a January scramble.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="mtd-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="mtd-title">Making Tax Digital isn't optional much longer</h2>
          <p>HMRC's rollout hits sole traders in three waves, and the next one is the biggest.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="mtd-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Mandatory from</th>
                <th scope="col">Qualifying income over</th>
                <th scope="col">Who's affected</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td data-label="Mandatory from">6 April 2026</td>
                <td data-label="Qualifying income over">£50,000</td>
                <td data-label="Who's affected">~780,000 sole traders &amp; landlords, already live</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td data-label="Mandatory from">6 April 2027</td>
                <td data-label="Qualifying income over">£30,000</td>
                <td data-label="Who's affected">~970,000 more traders</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td data-label="Mandatory from">6 April 2028</td>
                <td data-label="Qualifying income over">£20,000</td>
                <td data-label="Who's affected">The core of the sole-trader market</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mtd-note">Trade Forge keeps the digital records HMRC-recognised software needs, as a by-product of running your day-to-day jobs, not a separate task.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="pricing-title">One plan. No contract.</h2>
        </div>
        <article class="price-card">
          <p class="offer">First 100 sign-ups: 3 months free</p>
          <p class="amount">£29.99<span>/month</span></p>
          <ul class="price-list">
            <li>Unlimited WhatsApp bookings &amp; quotes</li>
            <li>Full job pipeline, booked to paid</li>
            <li>Invoices &amp; payment reminders</li>
            <li>MTD-ready quarterly exports</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-full" href={whatsappUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Join the waitlist on WhatsApp
          </a>
        </article>
      </section>

      <footer>
        Built by tradespeople for UK sole traders.
        <strong>Trade Forge</strong>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
